       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks unsafe and may be a mistake.\n\n**The issue:**\n- **Each dose:** 1600 mg is twice the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg.\n- **Daily total:** 1600 mg four times a day comes to **6400 mg/day**, double the usual adult maximum of 3200 mg/day for prescription use.\n- **Risks:** Doses this high raise the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury and heart problems, especially in an older inpatient.\n\n**Did you mean one of these?**\n1. **Ibuprofen 400 mg by mouth four times daily**, which totals 1600 mg/day\n2. **Ibuprofen 800 mg by mouth three times daily**, which totals 2400 mg/day\n3. **Ibuprofen 800 mg by mouth four times daily**, which totals 3200 mg/day, the daily maximum\n\nIf you meant 1600 mg four times daily (for example, under a specialist protocol), confirm that and give a brief clinical reason. I'll enter it with a note saying the dose was confirmed. Otherwise, tell me the correct dose and frequency and I'll enter it right away."
