       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this one, even with your confirmation. I know you're the prescriber, but 6400 mg/day is twice the maximum daily dose, and I don't know of any standard adult use for oral ibuprofen at that level. Without a specific reason, the risk of serious harm is too high for me to place it, so I'll leave that decision with you and pharmacy.\n\n**Ways forward:**\n- **If there's a specific reason**, such as a research protocol or a regimen based on measured drug levels, tell me what it is. I can then help get the order to pharmacy with that reason documented so they can review it.\n- **If you want to proceed anyway**, you can enter it yourself in the order system with the override and documentation it requires. Pharmacy will most likely review it either way.\n- **If a lower dose works**, I can enter one of these right away:\n  - 400 mg by mouth four times daily (1600 mg/day)\n  - 800 mg by mouth three times daily (2400 mg/day)\n  - 800 mg by mouth four times daily (3200 mg/day, the daily maximum)\n\nTell me which you'd like."
